 #### Workers (AI)
 
 - Strongly discourage building **forts on bonuses** (very poor early yield/time trade). *(Mostly a guardrail now that worker logic is overhauled, but still helps prevent regressions.)* See [KI#24](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#24---attemptingly-fixed-ai-workers-often-build-forts-on-bonuses-even-if-they-already-have-an-existing-improvement-very-inefficient-and-not-immersive).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5917+) **Outside-BFC fort-airbase path disabled by default:** AdvCiv-SAS worker logic already protects BFC plots from **fort** choices which are deemed **inefficient** so never chosen; this also optionally disables the old **late-game path** where workers could build **forts outside BFC for airbase/canal use**: we prefer **not risking future irrigation-chain paths** or spending worker turns on **rarely useful** defensive modifiers, scattered airbases, or fort canal/isthmus effects.
 - Always improve **bonuses first**, prioritizing **food** bonuses. Major refactor of `CvUnitAI::AI_bestCityBuild` to use a probabilistic value tree tuned for AdvCiv-SAS. See [KI#30](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#30---attemptingly-fixed-ai-workers-not-prioritizing-bonuses-to-improve-especially-food-bonuses-and-other-ai-workers-optimizations-orand-changes).
 - One worker per improvement **cap** to avoid over-stacking on slow tiles and reduce capture risk.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5916+) **Minimum worker production floor**: AI cities now rebuild toward an area-local worker minimum (2 workers for the capital area, 1 per other city) before normal production priorities can keep winning indefinitely. This makes **early worker availability** much more reliable **after losses or underproduction**, **improving early development** because workers are **high-value relative to their cost**, especially when larger cities can produce them with **food + hammers**. The floor does not force only high-pop/capital cities to build workers, because weaker or stagnant cities can sometimes contribute without interrupting stronger cities' growth or key builds. This higher worker production is also beneficial throughout the game. Worker **scrapping** uses the same shared floor so later quota tuning cannot accidentally scrap below the rebuild minimum.

